---The Inventory table provides access to Inv objects.
---@class Inventory
Inventory = {}

---Returns the Inv associated with the supplied InvType.
---@param config InvType A valid InvType.
---@return Inv # The inventory container for a list of objects.
---@overload fun(id: integer): Inv
function Inventory.Find(config) end

---An inventory provides access to a list of InvSlot entries, each of which contains information about the ObjType
---contained within it. Inventories are of a fixed size, and their slots may or may not be populated by an InvSlot.
---
---Info: An `Inv` object is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Warning: Use `Inv.isValid` to confirm that an inventory still exists before trying to access its properties.
---Inventories can be added or removed from the client by the server for a variety of reasons e.g. the player closes a
---shop interface. When an inventory's data is removed it will become invalid, and any copies of this usertype should be
---disposed of. If the same inventory data is re-added to the client by the server, such as walking back into visibility
---range, then a different new Inv object will be created.
---@class Inv
---@field id integer (Read-only) Unique ID associated with the inventory.
---@field config InvType (Read-only) InvType config used to construct the inventory.
---@field isValid boolean (Read-only) Is the inventory object valid.
---@field slotCount integer (Read-only) Total number of slots.
---@field usedSlotCount integer (Read-only) Number of non-empty slots.
---@field freeSlotCount integer (Read-only) Number of empty slots.
local Inv = {}

---Returns the InvSlot at the specified index.
---
---Warning: This function returns a copy of the data in the specified slot at the time of execution.
---
---In the client: It never returns nil: a slot outside the inventory is an empty slot, whose obj has the id -1 and whose
---count is 0.
---@param index integer A valid slot index. Index values are 1-indexed.
---@return InvSlot
function Inv:GetSlot(index) end

---Returns the current data associated for all slots in the inventory.
---
---Warning: This function returns a copy of the data in the specified slot at the time of execution.
---@return InvSlot[]
function Inv:GetSlots() end

---Returns the number of objects matching a valid ObjType specified in the associated inventory.
---@param objType ObjType A valid ObjType.
---@return integer # The number of objects matching the specified ObjType.
---@overload fun(self: Inv, id: integer): integer
function Inv:GetTotal(objType) end

---Returns the number of objects in the inventory that are in the category specified.
---@param category integer A valid category of object.
---@return integer # The number of objects matching the specified category.
function Inv:GetCategoryTotal(category) end

